1. Assignment Overview
Title: Mini E-Commerce Application
Goal
The goal of this assignment is to build a simple e-commerce mobile application using Flutter.
Students will create a multi-screen application that displays products by category and allows
users to navigate from the homepage to category pages and individual product-detail pages.
The assignment focuses on developing practical understanding of Flutter UI components,
layouts, scrolling, reusable widgets, external packages, cards, stacks, buttons, and
navigation.
Students are not required to implement backend, authentication, payment, cart
management, or database functionality.
The application should use static/local product data.

2. Learning Objectives
After completing this assignment, students should be able to:
● Create a Flutter application using MaterialApp and Scaffold.
● Design an application using AppBar.
● Create horizontal and vertical scrolling layouts.
● Create reusable product cards.
● Use Container, Card, Padding, Row, Column, and Stack.
● Display images inside product cards.
● Use buttons and interactive widgets.
● Implement navigation between multiple screens.
● Pass product information from one screen to another.
● Use a package from pub.dev.
● Create a carousel/banner section.
● Create category-based product layouts.
● Create a product-detail screen.
● Organize Flutter code into reusable widgets and screens.

