28. Final Application Flow: The expected
final flow is:

Expected Learning Outcome
By the end of this assignment, students should have built their first complete multi-screen
Flutter application, rather than isolated widget exercises.
The progression is intentional:
Widgets → Layout → Scrolling → Reusable Components → External Packages →
Cards → Stack → Navigation → Data Passing → Multi-screen Application
This also sets up the next stage nicely: Cart + state management, where students can take
this same e-commerce project and introduce shared state, models, and eventually a local
database/API.